<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! oracle.cast.throws ~ an alias record, forwarding to oracle.library.consults

The address `lar:///oracle.cast.throws` re-keyed to `lar:///oracle.library.consults` when the oracle family dropped its special case: one affordance consults any oracle whose corpus rests on a library shelf, the kind riding as data (moolelo 2026-11-26, "The oracle family, re-keyed"). Every rename carries a signed alias record (Domain Affordances law 4), so a grant, a note or a cast record that names the old address keeps pointing at what its giver meant.

The record takes the forwarder's shape a rename leaves: `forward-to` names the carrier's new seat, and the body transcludes it. `alias-from` and `alias-to` name the two bare addresses; its tags hold both, so `[tag[lar:///oracle.cast.throws]]` still gathers this record and every cast landed before the re-key. The frame's block check seals the record and the commit that lands it signs it. The record grants nothing: a carrier describes, the door checks the ocap (law 1).

{{lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/oracle.library.consults}}

